From 6efea7d7019c1869dcca78ae558ce8c64ddeaa43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 12:45:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0149 -- wave-53
 skip-redundant-clearScreen lever

Per flush-instr's docs/internal/WAVE-53-CLEAR-INTO-BACKDROP-DESIGN.md
(MODEX-DECISION-AND-FPS-LEVER-PLAN.md sec.5.7 lever 3). The wave-53
PERF lever; ships in the wave-53 binary alongside the 0148 Logger+LOGS
hygiene ride-along (0149 applies after 0148; different code, no
conflict).

DEFAULT-ON. Cycle-1 shipped this default-OFF (strict-"1" opt-in) for
the 4-cell A/B; after real-HW validation (+1.02 fps, mechanism-
verified, build-qa pixel-identical SKIP=0-vs-=1 on the canonical
scene; user-approved promotion 2026-05-15) the default was flipped to
ON with a strict-"0" killswitch, matching the bg-skip / mds-clear-LUT
default-ON lever convention.

WHY DOS NEEDS THIS: per the wave-52 log analysis, on scrolling frames
DrawScene() memsets the full 76800-byte framebuffer
(clearScreen(BLACK), ~2.40 ms median on the scrolling cluster) and
then redraws a full-screen opaque backdrop over it -- the clear is
pure redundant bandwidth. On the canonical Mimiga BK_PARALLAX KPI
scene ~67% of frames are scrolling.

LEVER: skip DrawScene's clearScreen(BLACK) when the backdrop pass will
provably repaint EVERY screen row this frame.

THE ESSENTIAL CORRECTNESS RULE (design sec.1): map_draw_backdrop
for FIXED/PARALLAX/FOLLOWFG has a default-ON sub-region partial-blit
mode (patch 0130, BG_SUBREGION_BLIT) -- the backdrop does NOT always
cover the full screen. The skip predicate must NEVER trust patch
0130's FG-occlusion table for clear-coverage; it skips the clear ONLY
when the BACKDROP itself paints every row. A false-positive in the
FG-occlusion table therefore can never produce stale-frame garbage --
worst case the lever fires too rarely, never wrongly.

IMPLEMENTATION:
- New helper map_clear_is_redundant() in map.cpp. Returns true iff
  ALL of: (1) map.scrolltype in {BK_FIXED, BK_PARALLAX, BK_FOLLOWFG,
  BK_HIDE, BK_HIDE2, BK_HIDE3} -- the full-screen-coverage scrolltypes;
  BK_FASTLEFT / BK_FASTLEFT_LAYERS / NOFALLLEFT excluded (coverage not
  guaranteed). (2) !flipacceltime -- the backdrop pass is gated on
  !flipacceltime in DrawScene; if set, the backdrop does not draw, so
  the clear is required. (3) backdrop[map.backdrop] loaded -- the
  backdrop pass early-returns on a missing asset; N/A for BK_HIDE*
  (the HIDE handler self-does a full clearScreen regardless, so HIDE*
  is allowed through on (1)+(2) alone). (4) the backdrop covers the
  FULL screen -- BG_SUBREGION_BLIT disabled OR its computed
  [bg_top,bg_bot] range == whole screen. Clause 4 calls
  _compute_bg_visible_yrange() -- the same pre-draw computation patch
  0130 runs inside map_draw_backdrop; calling it from the predicate
  warms its (curmap,mapy_tile) cache so the subsequent
  map_draw_backdrop call hits it -- one computation per frame, no
  added cost.
- Call-site change in game.cpp DrawScene: the existing clear guard
  `if (!bg_skip_unchanged)` becomes
  `if (!bg_skip_unchanged && !(skip_redundant_clear_enabled() &&
  map_clear_is_redundant()))`. The existing bg_skip_unchanged
  (static-frame, patch 0143) path is untouched -- this adds only the
  scrolling-frame skip. The MdsClearTimer scope is kept intact so
  [mds-decomp-stat phase=mds_clear] keeps sample-count parity.
- Killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SKIP_REDUNDANT_CLEAR: DEFAULT-ON,
  strict-"0" to disable. Sentinel-cached on first call (the
  _backdrop_cache_is_disabled() idiom) -- never a per-flip getenv.
  When killswitched off the && short-circuits before
  map_clear_is_redundant() is evaluated.

CORRECTNESS: the only frames affected are scrolling frames where
map_clear_is_redundant() proves full backdrop coverage; the backdrop
(or, for BK_HIDE*, the HIDE handler's own clearScreen) repaints every
row, so no stale pixels can surface. The predicate's clause 4 is the
conservative form -- it never trusts the FG-occlusion table, only the
backdrop's own coverage. Cross-map visual gate (BK_PARALLAX / BK_HIDE*
fire correctly; BK_FASTLEFT* never fire) is build-qa's promotion gate.

BK_HIDE* note: skipping DrawScene's clear for HIDE* eliminates a
genuinely redundant FIRST clear (the HIDE handler self-clears -- two
full clears -> one), net positive, zero risk.

FILES: src/map.h (2 decls), src/map.cpp (skip_redundant_clear_enabled
+ map_clear_is_redundant), src/game.cpp (the DrawScene clear-guard
term).

MEASURED: +1.02 fps real-HW (wave-53 4-cell PLAY3-vs-PLAY4), within
the design's +1.0-1.6 fps predicted band. Pixel-identical on the
canonical scene.

Single-mechanism per [[single_lever_per_binary_or_else_attribution_
impossible]]: the toggled lever is "skip the redundant scrolling-frame
clear". The 0148 Logger+LOGS hygiene patch rides in the same wave-53
binary, baked into all 4 PLAY cells, so it does not contaminate the
lever-3 A/B.

Banner regex for tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh BANNERS:
"map: skip-redundant-clear lever (ENABLED|DISABLED)"
